WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.660
At this point, Netflix is an entertainment
staple and a full-fledged cultural phenomenon.

00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:09.470
And you may think you have it all figured
out, but there are plenty of tricks to help

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:12.870
you take your night-in experience to the next
level.

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:17.109
So get on in your couch groove and prepare
to binge.

00:00:17.109 --> 00:00:22.289
Here are the Netflix hacks you'll want to
try ASAP.

00:00:22.289 --> 00:00:23.289
Category codes

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:28.630
Netflix's recommended categories can get old
pretty quickly, and those old fallbacks just

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.759
don't have the spark they used to.

00:00:30.759 --> 00:00:35.710
Get familiar with sub-category codes, which
give you access to more specific films, like

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:39.420
"Dramas Starring Colin Firth" or "Greek movies."

00:00:39.420 --> 00:00:44.130
There's a list seemingly a mile long, so you're
essentially guaranteed to land on something

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:46.340
you'll love, no matter how obscure.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:52.470
"I decided I would use my new Kung Fu powers
to fight crime so I became the best cop in

00:00:52.470 --> 00:00:53.630
the world.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:55.970
I became Kung Fury."

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:57.730
Highest quality

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:58.730
We've all been there.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:03.540
You're trying to watch something on Netflix,
but the quality keeps going out the window.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:12.280
Life just...it loses all meaning after that.

00:01:12.299 --> 00:01:16.680
Well, you may not be getting the best out
of your default Netflix settings.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:21.819
Squeeze the best quality out of your subscription
by customizing your playback settings to always

00:01:21.819 --> 00:01:23.570
stream in high definition.

00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:27.939
Head into "Account," then "My Profile," and
then "Playback Settings."

00:01:27.939 --> 00:01:29.679
Here, you have some choices.

00:01:29.679 --> 00:01:35.710
Choose between "Auto," which is the default
setting; "Low," for basic video quality; "Medium,"

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:42.400
for standard playback; or "High," which plays
all your films and TV shows in crisp HD.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:44.619
Hotkeys

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:46.430
Watching Netflix on your computer?

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.159
Netflix has some built-in hotkeys to make
your viewing experience easier.

00:01:50.159 --> 00:01:54.359
You can press "F" to go full-screen, and hit
Escape to return to normal.

00:01:54.359 --> 00:01:59.259
Pressing enter or the space bar will allow
you to pause, and "M" mutes the video.

00:01:59.259 --> 00:02:05.429
You can also rewind or fast forward in ten-second
increments by using the left and right keys.

00:02:05.429 --> 00:02:07.399
Clear out "Continue Watching"

00:02:07.399 --> 00:02:12.000
It's great to be able to go back and finish
shows and movies later, but that "Continue

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:15.760
Watching" queue can get seriously bogged down
over time.

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:18.600
When are you ever going to finish watching
Boyhood?

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.450
And that last season of Dexter was WEAK.

00:02:21.450 --> 00:02:26.690
Fortunately, it's easy to keep your "Continue
Watching" queue nice and organized by getting

00:02:26.690 --> 00:02:28.110
rid of random titles.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.830
Dive into "Account," then "My Profile," and
"Viewing Activity" to remove any shows you've

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.830
stopped watching.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:40.190
Click the tiny "X" near each title you'd rather
forget you watched, and Netflix will clear

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:44.380
it from the list, allowing you to get back
to the things you're really interested in.

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.980
"That's a laser raptor, I thought they went
extinct thousands of years ago."

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.920
Kill all spoilers

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:56.340
You know what's the worst?

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:57.340
Spoilers.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:03:01.840
You're blazing through Twin Peaks or Breaking
Bad when you glance at the next episode's

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.760
description, and suddenly Making a Murderer
just got a lot more literal.

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:12.790
Fortunately, you can fight back with Flix
Plus, a Google Chrome extension that works

00:03:12.790 --> 00:03:17.530
with Netflix to blur out any hidden spoilers
in film and TV show blurbs.

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:24.450
So sit back, relax, and let your favorite
characters do all the killing, spoiler-free.

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:26.350
Try new features

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.380
Netflix is constantly developing improvements
and enhancements and testing them in real

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:32.740
time with real-life people.

00:03:32.740 --> 00:03:37.830
Take new features out for a spin before anyone
else by going to "Account," then "Settings,"

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:39.600
and "Test Participation."

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:45.430
Enrolling is as simple as shifting the "include
me in tests and previews" option to "on."

00:03:45.430 --> 00:03:49.530
You may even get your hands on the feature
that changes Netflix forever, months before

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:52.000
the general public does.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:53.460
Control your account

00:03:53.460 --> 00:03:59.380
These days, Netflix accounts get passed around
faster than earplugs at a Dave Matthews concert.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:04.240
You give your login to a few friends, and
suddenly, you've lost track entirely of everyone

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.240
on your plan.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:10.100
If you've had multiple people using your Netflix
account in the past, see who's still benefiting

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:16.310
from your monthly payment by checking "Account,"
then "Viewing Activity," and clicking "See

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:18.090
recent account access."

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:20.150
Do things look strange?

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:24.250
Is Aunt Gertrude watching Knitting Wars out
in Iowa again?

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:29.930
Take back the gift that keeps on giving by
signing out of all currently logged-in devices.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:31.650
4K viewing

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:35.620
We've all heard that beauty is in the eye
of the beholder.

00:04:35.620 --> 00:04:42.150
Well, Netflix has taken note and started introducing
4K titles to its library under certain subscription

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:43.150
plans.

00:04:43.150 --> 00:04:47.920
If you've got a 4K T-V and a strong internet
connection, and want to get the most out of

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:55.790
your hardware, just type "4K" into the Netflix
search box to browse Netflix's Ultra HD library.

00:04:55.790 --> 00:04:56.790
Rating control

00:04:56.790 --> 00:05:01.310
You're probably already aware that Netflix
caters its suggestions to you based on your

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:07.030
watch history, but you can tell Netflix what
you really want to watch by going to "Account,"

00:05:07.030 --> 00:05:10.680
and then "Ratings" under the "My Profile"
section.

00:05:10.680 --> 00:05:16.400
Here, you can alter or remove ratings to fine-tune
your Netflix recommendations.

00:05:16.400 --> 00:05:18.200
Watch offline

00:05:18.200 --> 00:05:23.720
We've all had a time when we wanted to watch
Netflix without an internet connection.

00:05:23.720 --> 00:05:28.011
Maybe you're on a long flight and itching
to binge some Black Mirror, or you're out

00:05:28.011 --> 00:05:31.800
getting in touch with nature but get bored
with the dumb flowers.

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:33.610
Well, you're in luck.

00:05:33.610 --> 00:05:38.190
There are a number of films and series ready
for download in Netflix's library, but this

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.850
feature is only accessible on iOS and Android
devices.

00:05:42.850 --> 00:05:47.200
All you have to do is install the Netflix
app on your phone or tablet, and when you

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:52.680
log in, you'll be greeted with a "Download
&amp; Go" splash-page, where you can tap "Find

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:53.740
something to download."

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:59.030
Alternatively, you can make your way to the
main menu, where you'll find the "Available

00:05:59.030 --> 00:06:00.750
for Download" section.

00:06:00.750 --> 00:06:06.230
Tap the arrow button to save to your device,
and you're all set for offline-viewing!

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:08.610
Outside opinion

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:12.480
Next time you're about to spend two hours
on a movie you're not sure about, check out

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:13.620
Rotten Tomatoes first.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:19.150
The site's "On DVD and Streaming" section
collects everything available on Netflix,

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:23.449
plus a ton of other streaming services, so
you can browse ratings to weed out anything

00:06:23.449 --> 00:06:25.240
that's guaranteed to be awful.

00:06:25.240 --> 00:06:31.210
The site also has a list of new releases hitting
Netflix soon, so you can always pick a winner.

00:06:31.210 --> 00:06:32.270
Thanks for watching!

00:06:32.270 --> 00:06:35.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:35.420 --> 00:06:38.120
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

